        <h2>Regional Variations Worth Seeking Out</h2>

        <p><strong>Jaffna rice and curry:</strong> The northern Tamil rice and curry is the most distinct regional variation — less coconut milk, stronger dry spicing, the use of palmyra palm vinegar and dried fish in ways that are specific to this region. A banana leaf meal (served on a fresh banana leaf rather than a plate) in Jaffna is one of the best eating experiences in Sri Lanka.</p>

        <p><strong>South coast fish curries:</strong> Coastal areas around Galle, Unawatuna and Tangalle produce some of the best fish curries in the country — fresh reef fish, crab or prawn cooked in a dark, coconut-rich gravy. The best versions are found at the simple restaurants near the fish markets, not the beachfront tourist strip.</p>

        <p><strong>Hill country rice and curry:</strong> The highlands around Kandy, Nuwara Eliya and Ella produce excellent vegetables — leeks, beans, potatoes — that make the vegetable curries particularly good. The meals here tend to be slightly heartier, reflecting the cooler climate.</p>

