        <h2>Vegetarian and Vegan Rice and Curry</h2>

        <p>Sri Lankan rice and curry is one of the best choices for vegetarians in Asia. The vast majority of the components — dhal, vegetable curries, pol sambol, rice, papadum — are plant-based. The main issue is Maldive fish (umbalakada), which is added to pol sambol and seeni sambol as a flavour base and appears in some vegetable curries. If you are strictly vegan, tell the restaurant you want "no Maldive fish" (umbalakada netthuva) — most can easily accommodate this, especially in Buddhist areas.</p>

        <p>Purely vegetarian rice and curry restaurants (marked "pure veg" or "saivam") are common in Tamil-majority areas of the north and east and in the Cultural Triangle.</p>

